WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.421
FaMED Prep helps you practise the medical German you

00:00:04.421 --> 00:00:08.843
need in patient conversations, clinical handovers, and written documentation.

00:00:09.967 --> 00:00:14.413
Anamnese. Aufklärung. Arzt zu Arzt. Arztbrief.

00:00:15.533 --> 00:00:18.421
Start with a fictional patient. Ask your questions in

00:00:18.421 --> 00:00:21.309
German, listen to the patient’s response, and use what

00:00:21.309 --> 00:00:24.197
you hear to decide your next question. Here is

00:00:24.197 --> 00:00:27.084
a short example.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:31.284
Guten Tag, Herr Müller. Mein Name ist Doktor Weber.

00:00:31.284 --> 00:00:34.368
Ich würde gerne mit Ihnen über Ihre Beschwerden sprechen.

00:00:34.368 --> 00:00:37.452
Was führt Sie heute zu uns?

00:00:37.452 --> 00:00:40.305
Guten Tag. Ich habe in den letzten drei Monaten

00:00:40.305 --> 00:00:43.158
ungewollt etwa zehn Kilo abgenommen, mein Stuhlgang hat sich

00:00:43.158 --> 00:00:46.012
verändert, und manchmal ist Blut im Stuhl.

00:00:47.533 --> 00:00:50.813
Seit wann haben Sie diese Beschwerden? Können Sie mir

00:00:50.813 --> 00:00:54.093
bitte beschreiben, wie sich Ihr Stuhlgang verändert hat?

00:00:54.093 --> 00:00:57.053
Das fing vor etwa drei Monaten an, zuerst mit

00:00:57.053 --> 00:01:00.013
dem Stuhlgang, dann kam der Gewichtsverlust dazu. Beides, im

00:01:00.013 --> 00:01:02.973
Wechsel. Ein paar Tage Durchfall, dann wieder ein paar

00:01:02.973 --> 00:01:05.933
Tage Verstopfung.

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:11.120
After the conversation, review percentages for grammar, fluency and

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:14.806
structure, and clarity. In this six-question demo, the feedback

00:01:14.806 --> 00:01:18.493
flags a repeated question. Use these transcript-based practice ratings

00:01:18.493 --> 00:01:22.179
and comments to practise listening closely and asking a

00:01:22.179 --> 00:01:25.866
better follow-up.

00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:30.302
In Aufklärung, practise explaining a procedure to a patient.

00:01:30.302 --> 00:01:33.638
Read your role and the case first. Then give

00:01:33.638 --> 00:01:36.973
a clear explanation of what is planned, what the

00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:40.309
patient should know, and what questions remain.

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:45.090
The full-test feedback separates content, structure, and grammar. Review

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:48.747
what you included, how you organised it, and which

00:01:48.747 --> 00:01:52.404
language points need another attempt.

00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:56.822
In Arzt–Arzt, practise presenting a patient to a colleague.

00:01:56.822 --> 00:02:00.111
Work from the case information, select the relevant facts,

00:02:00.111 --> 00:02:03.401
and explain your assessment and proposed next steps in

00:02:03.401 --> 00:02:06.690
a structured handover.

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:11.817
The full test gives feedback on structure, content, linguistic

00:02:11.817 --> 00:02:15.833
precision, and communication style. Use the comments to make

00:02:15.833 --> 00:02:19.850
your next presentation clearer and more focused.

00:02:20.967 --> 00:02:24.428
In Arztbrief, turn the information you hear into a

00:02:24.428 --> 00:02:27.888
written account. First listen to the practice case.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:37.000
[German practice-case audio excerpt]

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.906
Write the answer yourself. Work through the patient’s information

00:02:39.906 --> 00:02:42.812
in a sensible order, then submit your text for

00:02:42.812 --> 00:02:45.718
AI practice feedback. This example shows actual typing in

00:02:45.718 --> 00:02:48.623
the app.

00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:53.964
Review structure, completeness, medical terminology, grammar, and precision. Read

00:02:53.964 --> 00:02:58.194
the specific comments, choose one useful correction, and carry

00:02:58.194 --> 00:03:02.425
it into your next attempt.

00:03:03.533 --> 00:03:06.293
Choose one skill to work on today. Explore the

00:03:06.293 --> 00:03:09.052
available tasks at FaMED Prep, and build a practice

00:03:09.052 --> 00:03:11.812
routine you can repeat.

